Z||000000||Mattsfiero||10-06-2000||08:18 AM||||Okay here is the thing my car has made a few changes on it's own. First strange event was when I went to turn my car off in the cold weather with my heat still on the heater remained on...However when I turned it off it stayed off untill I started the car again. The secound was with my fog lamps...I installed them using an add a fuse circuit wich plugs into the fuse and allows you to plug in another fuse. Okay well I choose the ten Amp fuse in the front of the box well it was a hot wire (Constant power) before I would forget to turn them off and now when I turn the car off they turn off. Now I think it might be my ignition Relay but have not a clue where it is. Does anyone know where it is or if it is?<P><BR>Matt<BR>85 custom base coupe<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
