Z||000003||StuGood||10-06-2000||12:43 PM||||I love (other peoples'!) electrical problems.<P>Heater blower - if it sticks on "high" speed only, I wonder if it's the high speed blower relay sticking.  <P>Don't think there <B>is</B> an "ignition relay" in a stock Fiero.  ||||reg||5
Z||000004||dman||10-06-2000||06:08 PM||||Hello everyone. I like StuGood's diagnosis. If the blower sticks when in the high position, it is most likely the blower relay. That relay's sole purpose is to drive the blower fan when you choose the "high" speed setting. This relay is located inside your front trunk area. Look by the blower fan (by the passenger side) and you will find two relays. The relay that is towards the drivers side is the one that activates the blower fan when you select the "high" speed.<P>To check that it is the proper relay simply remove it and everything should work normally except the high speed setting. If you remove the wrong relay then none of the blower fan settings will work. There's a little metal tab that holds the relay in place, pry (gently) on the tab and you should be able to pull upwards to remove the relay.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||10-06-2000||10:33 PM||||My blower fan sometimes continues to run after I have turned the ignition switch off. It has only done it once or twice though.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||10-06-2000||11:20 PM||||I just thought I would let you know that I had a problem like this on a another car, non Fiero, anyway, it turned out to be the ignition cylinder. Mine would shut the engine off but everything like the radio and A/C and heaters stayed on. It is just a possibility, but your problem sounds more like a problem in the individual system rather then one thing cause all the problems.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mattsfiero||10-07-2000||07:25 AM||||Thank you for the advice and I will check it today. It sounds like it makes sense the only other thing is the fuse link I used for the fog lamps all of a sudden acting off the ignition and figured it would be the relay. I will try the other module first though. Thank you all again.<P>------------------<BR>Matt<BR>85 custom coupe<BR>Mattsfiero@excite.com<BR>www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero||||reg||1
